Description: Report presses and releases of chosen modifier keys to GNOME Shell.
 GNOME Shell receives a key only when it is bound or while the Shell has the keyboard, so it cannot show what a
 modifier key does while the key is held, as a global menu does by underlining the letters of its menus while Alt is
 held, and it learns about a lone tap of a modifier only for the overlay key. meta_display_set_watched_modifiers()
 names modifier keys whose presses and releases the display reports with the signals watched-modifier-pressed, when
 the key is pressed while no other modifier is held, watched-modifier-combined, when another key or a pointer button
 is pressed while it is held, and watched-modifier-released, which says whether the key was tapped on its own. The
 keys still reach the focused window, and a press is not reported while the focused window inhibits shortcuts.
 .
 The test /core/keybindings/watched-modifiers of src/tests/keybindings.c checks the signals for a tap, for the key
 held together with another key, for a press while another modifier is held and for the other Alt key, which is
 not watched, and that nothing is reported once no key is watched.
